-Figure~\ref{fig:single-column} runs the four sweeps of
-Section~\ref{sec:robustness} for the nonlinear problem of
-Section~\ref{sec:nonlinear} again with both patches, now with
-$\delta = K\,\delta_{\mathrm{thr}}$, $K = 1$ unless swept (FGMRES to a
-relative residual of $10^{-6}$ and Newton to an absolute residual of
-$10^{-9}$, no Eisenstat--Walker forcing, six GMRES iterations per
-level preconditioned by the patch operator in place of the Richardson
-sweeps of Appendix~\ref{app:petsc-options}, two MPI ranks).  The
-single-column patch converges in every run in which the star patch
-converges, with totals at $K = 1$ between $10$ and $50$ against $3$
-to $40$: the robustness survives.  It costs iterations, and in three
-of the four sweeps the excess follows the constant: the ratio is
-largest for thin domains at small $\Delta t$ (panel~(a), $32$ against
-$3$ at $L_z = 250\,\mathrm{m}$, $\Delta t = 50\,\mathrm{s}$), it
-shrinks under horizontal refinement (panel~(b)), and over the $170$
-runs of the three parameter sweeps at $K = 1$ the ratio of the two
-counts falls with $\rho_1$ (panel~(d)), from a median of $5.2$ below
-$\rho_1 = 10^{-2}$ to $1.1$ above $\rho_1 = 10^{2}$.  Within the
-admissible range of the shift the ratio lies between $1.0$ and $3.3$
-at $K = 1$ and between $1.4$ and $5.5$ at $K = 0.1$ (panel~(c); $44$
-against $8$ at $\Delta t = 50\,\mathrm{s}$), so over the one decade
-tested below the threshold the full solver does not yet show the
-$K$-independence of Table~\ref{tab:single-column-block}; the two
-counts coincide only for $K \gtrsim 100$, outside that range, where
-the omitted runs show the outer iteration failing for both patches.
-Two further drawbacks are not predicted by the constant.  The growth
-with $N_z$ in panel~(b) ($20$ to $39$ at $\Delta t = 50\,\mathrm{s}$
-for $N_z = 10$ to $80$) is absent from the block solve of
-Table~\ref{tab:single-column-block}, and so must arise from the
-interaction of the inexact inner solve with the outer Newton--Krylov
-iteration; and, unlike the star counts, the single-column counts at
-$\Delta t \le 100\,\mathrm{s}$ vary by about $20\%$ between identical
-runs.  The smaller patch is a robust but markedly weaker approximation
-of $S^{-1}$.
